<Defs>

  <!-- Migrated from "Dog Collars" by Shenanigans (Workshop 2644644983, last supported 1.4),
       with "Patch Collar Malinois" by Annabelesca (3062026756) folded in - that mod was a
       verbatim copy of this one carrying a single extra animal, and shipped the same
       defNames, so installing both silently overwrote one with the other.

       Four things changed in the move from Animal Gear to Animal Apparel: Framework.

       1. bodyPartGroups: Neck -> AnimalNeck. The old framework grafted the HUMAN Neck group
          onto animal bodies; the new one knows only AnimalHead/AnimalBody/AnimalLegs.
          AnimalNeck is ours - see Defs/Bodies/BodyPartGroups_AnimalNeck.xml.

       2. tags: the marker <li>Animal</li> became <li>AnimalApparel</li> + <li>AnimalOnly</li>,
          and every bare animal name became <li>defNameXxx</li>, which is how the new
          framework restricts a wearable to particular animals.

       3. Every modded animal is now gated with MayRequire. This is not tidiness: the new
          framework resolves those tags through DefDatabase<ThingDef>.GetNamed(name, true),
          which logs an error for each name it cannot find - and it runs that on every
          apparel-optimisation check, for every pawn. Ungated, the 69 modded names in this
          file would have produced a continuous stream of errors for anyone not running all
          21 source mods.

       4. AnimalFallbackInvisible: the new framework logs an error when an animal is allowed
          to wear a piece for which no per-animal sprite exists. Of the 78 animals listed
          here, 77 have art; only SCCaucasianshepherd (Spidercamp's Dog Pack) does not, and
          it had none in the original either. This tag makes that case draw nothing instead
          of complaining, which is what the original did.

       drawData sets an explicit layer of 71. The framework hands every piece of animal
       apparel the same baseLayer, 70, taken from the single AnimalApparel node in the render
       tree, so without this a collar and a flak jacket would stack in whatever order the
       animal happened to put them on. 71 is one step above; PawnRenderNodeWorker.LayerFor
       treats drawData's layer as a replacement for baseLayer, not an offset. -->

	<ThingDef Name="DogBowBase" ParentName="ApparelMakeableBase" Abstract="True">
		<techLevel>Neolithic</techLevel>
		<recipeMaker>
			<researchPrerequisite />
			<recipeUsers>
				<li>ElectricTailoringBench</li>
				<li>HandTailoringBench</li>
				<li>CraftingSpot</li>
			</recipeUsers>
		</recipeMaker>
		<statBases>
			<WorkToMake>1000</WorkToMake>
			<MaxHitPoints>50</MaxHitPoints>
			<Mass>0.1</Mass>
			<Flammability>0.9</Flammability>
			<ArmorRating_Blunt>0.01</ArmorRating_Blunt>
			<ArmorRating_Sharp>0.05</ArmorRating_Sharp>
			<ArmorRating_Heat>0</ArmorRating_Heat>
			<StuffEffectMultiplierInsulation_Cold>0.05</StuffEffectMultiplierInsulation_Cold>
			<StuffEffectMultiplierInsulation_Heat>0.02</StuffEffectMultiplierInsulation_Heat>
			<EquipDelay>0.1</EquipDelay>
		</statBases>
		<stuffCategories>
			<li>Fabric</li>
		</stuffCategories>
		<colorGenerator Class="ColorGenerator_StandardApparel" />
		<graphicData>
			<texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/Apparel/Accessories/DogBow/dogbow</texPath>
			<graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
		</graphicData>
		<thingCategories>
			<li>Animal_Apparel</li>
		</thingCategories>
		<generateAllowChance>0</generateAllowChance>
		<apparel>
			<careIfWornByCorpse>false</careIfWornByCorpse>
			<bodyPartGroups>
				<li>AnimalNeck</li>
			</bodyPartGroups>
			<!-- A directory, not a file stem: the framework looks for
			     <wornGraphicPath>/<AnimalDefName>/<AnimalDefName>_[north|east|south].png -->
			<wornGraphicPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/Apparel/Accessories/DogBow</wornGraphicPath>
			<layers>
				<li>OnSkin</li>
			</layers>
			<drawData>
				<defaultData>
					<layer>71</layer>
				</defaultData>
			</drawData>
			<defaultOutfitTags>
				<li>Anything</li>
			</defaultOutfitTags>
			<canBeDesiredForIdeo>false</canBeDesiredForIdeo>
		</apparel>
		<modExtensions>
			<li Class="AnimalGear.AnimalApparelDefExtension">
				<showCoverageForBodyType>QuadrupedAnimalWithPaws</showCoverageForBodyType>
			</li>
		</modExtensions>
	</ThingDef>

